# GitHub Linguist Configuration
# This file tells GitHub to recognize this as a HIP/C++ project

# Treat .hip files as C++ for proper syntax highlighting and language detection
*.hip linguist-language=HIP

# Mark Python management script as vendored (supporting tool, not primary code)
traffic_manager.py linguist-vendored

# Mark HTML as documentation (so it doesn't dominate language stats)
*.html linguist-documentation

# Mark JSON output files as generated
*.json linguist-generated

# Optionally: Mark Python as a supporting language (not documentation)
#*.py linguist-detectable

# Mark README as documentation
README.md linguist-documentation
